00:41:47.546 --> 00:41:49.810
That's a waste.


00:41:49.849 --> 00:41:52.317
OK, let's run the offense!


00:41:53.753 --> 00:41:56.551
- Without a ball?
- Yeah, without the ball, Clarence.


00:41:56.589 --> 00:41:58.887
Let's go, everybody get in position.


00:41:58.924 --> 00:42:02.860
- Patch that ball up, Scootsie.
- Come on! Hustle!


00:42:02.895 --> 00:42:04.920
OK, Clarence, flash through the lane.


00:42:04.964 --> 00:42:07.660
- Hustle, Clarence!
- Come on, come on.


00:42:07.700 --> 00:42:08.689
Ball, ball, ball!


00:42:08.734 --> 00:42:11.396
We been runnin'
the same play all day.


00:42:11.437 --> 00:42:13.530
Yeah, can we maybe try
play number two?


00:42:13.572 --> 00:42:16.803
No! I want you to be brain-dead,
gentlemen!


00:42:16.842 --> 00:42:20.869
'Cause someday you're gonna be
too tired or too nervous to think.


00:42:20.913 --> 00:42:24.314
And when you are,
this is the play that I'm gonna call.


00:42:24.350 --> 00:42:27.046
We need to be able to run
this play in our sleep.


00:42:27.086 --> 00:42:29.646
I'm a rover, Coach.
I'm just gonna go rover.


00:42:29.688 --> 00:42:32.282
No, don't just go rovin'.
Run the play, Jackie Moon.


00:42:32.324 --> 00:42:33.882
I'm creatin' a diversion, though...


00:42:33.926 --> 00:42:36.656
- by runnin' in circles over here.
- Don't lose your mind, Jackie Moon.


00:42:36.695 --> 00:42:38.663
We are runnin' this until we puke.


00:42:38.697 --> 00:42:41.689
- Well, basically, we have.
- Yeah, I'm pretty beat, Coach.


00:42:41.734 --> 00:42:44.032
"Until we puke"
is not a figure of speech.


00:42:44.069 --> 00:42:46.003
We are literally going to puke.


00:42:46.038 --> 00:42:47.733
What does he mean by "literally"?


00:42:51.877 --> 00:42:54.243
I wish you were still
a washing machine!


00:42:54.280 --> 00:42:57.875
Get up and run, Coach!
You're gonna puke like everybody else!


00:42:57.917 --> 00:43:02.183
I can't puke, Monix!
I've never puked in my life, ever!


00:43:02.221 --> 00:43:03.449
You're lying to me.


00:43:03.489 --> 00:43:07.186
I've been sick before, I've just never
puked. Swear on my mother's grave.


00:43:07.226 --> 00:43:10.855
What about when you were a baby?
Babies throw up all the time.


00:43:10.896 --> 00:43:14.457
My mom said I never did it. I swear.


00:43:15.668 --> 00:43:17.602
She said I was fascinating.


00:43:17.636 --> 00:43:22.005
In fact, the local PBS wanted to do
a documentary on me.


00:43:23.843 --> 00:43:25.606
Have you ever been punched
in the jejunum?


00:43:25.644 --> 00:43:27.544
No, what's a jejunum?


00:43:27.580 --> 00:43:29.775
It's part of the small intestine.


00:43:29.815 --> 00:43:31.510
I don't think so.


00:43:31.550 --> 00:43:35.953
I mean, I've been punched in the armpit
before, and in the wrist twice.


00:43:36.722 --> 00:43:40.715
Coccyx, and in the back of the knee.


00:43:41.260 --> 00:43:44.855
Both eyes, and I've been punched
right in my tracheal...


00:44:03.716 --> 00:44:06.048
Let that out.


00:44:07.186 --> 00:44:09.484
Go ahead, Jackie. Just let it go.


00:44:12.258 --> 00:44:13.657
Hey, hey, hey.


00:44:16.996 --> 00:44:19.658
Get ahold of yourself, Jackie!


00:44:19.698 --> 00:44:23.498
Let go! Hold it in, Jackie!
Hold it in!


00:44:23.536 --> 00:44:25.561
Get off me, God damn it!


00:44:25.604 --> 00:44:26.969
Jackie!


00:44:33.412 --> 00:44:36.506
We are seeing a very different Tropics
